<title>CANADA: Toronto-Dominion Bank Q2 net profits rise.</title>
<headline>Toronto-Dominion Bank Q2 net profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			 C$0.76		   C$0.69</p>
<p> Net			240,000		  220,000</p>
<p> Assets	     153,206,000	    117,418,000</p>
<p> Deposits	    98,699,000	     80,573,000</p>
<p> Loans		 77,638,000	     68,026,000</p>
<p>			6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			 C$1.59		   C$1.39</p>
<p> Net		  504,000,000	    442,000,000</p>
<p>	 (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1997 figures include a C$29 million after-tax cost related to the TD's acquisition of Australian discount broker, Pont Securities Limited.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
</text>
